behind — `design/spike-2026-09-23.md:3`).

| item | verdict | evidence | command |
|---|---|---|---|
| **(a)** the hosted provider-set PUBLICATION path | **GAP → S01** | The only publish command is `apps/runner/src/dev-provider-set-publish-cli.ts` (31 lines), wired at `package.json:31`; it imports `developmentConfiguredProviderPanel` at `:12` and its publisher hard-codes `deployment: "local"` at `apps/runner/src/dev-deployment-register.ts:873`. `buildConfiguredProviderSetDeploymentRow` (`packages/register/src/configured-provider-set.ts:177`) has NO shipped caller — the tree states it at `tests/unit/v9-configured-provider-set-deployment.test.ts:209-211`. The kit states it at `deploy/vps/README.md:862` ("There is no hosted publish command yet."). No `production:` ref exists. What IS built, and is not this slice's work, is the enforcement door: `packages/register/src/configured-provider-set.ts:127-144`, pinned by `tests/unit/v9-configured-provider-set-deployment.test.ts:225` ("a hosted publication carries the vetted row or none at all"). | `git grep -n publishGeneral -- apps deploy tests` · `git grep -n '"production:' -- apps packages` · `git grep -n buildConfiguredProviderSetDeploymentRow -- apps packages tests` |
| **(b)** README §11's hosted provider-target example | **GAP → S03** | The member table at `deploy/vps/README.md:841-846` and the worked example at `:848-849` carry no price members, which both services require in hosted mode (`apps/api/src/main.ts:312`, `apps/runner/src/main.ts:87`). The refusal table at `:770-782` carries none of the six codes the kit's own notice names at `:25-27`. The pin that should have caught it reads ONE constant of three codes (`tests/unit/v9-provider-credential-files.test.ts:394-435` over `packages/providers/src/index.ts:740-744`), while `packages/providers/src/index.ts:727-731` claims the table "cannot drift". | `git grep -n input_price_micros_per_million -- deploy/vps/README.md` · `git grep -n 'PROVIDER_TARGET_PRICE_REQUIRED\|COST_ENVELOPE_POLICY_UNRESOLVED' -- deploy/vps/README.md` |
| **(c)** the localhost composition never declares the mode | **GAP → S02** | `DEBATEAI_DEPLOYMENT_MODE` appears in `deploy/vps/env/{api,runner}.env.example:14/:11`, in the loader (`packages/register/src/runtime-environment.ts:305`, `:569`) and in test fixtures (`tests/support/apiEnvironmentFixture.ts:12,46`) — and in ZERO files under `apps/`. It is absent from `DEVELOPMENT_API_ENVIRONMENT_KEYS` (`apps/runner/src/dev-api-environment.ts:36-65`). Local is therefore the absent-outside-production DEFAULT (`packages/register/src/runtime-environment.ts:85`), pinned by `tests/unit/v9-deployment-mode.test.ts:264`. | `git grep -n DEBATEAI_DEPLOYMENT_MODE -- apps packages deploy tests` |
| **(d)** a paid-endpoint probe cost guard | **GAP in the mechanism · UNVERIFIED in the need → no slice; documented by S03 R3.6 and routed as `V-ROW: NEW` below** | `probeFreshnessMs` comes from the `panelDiscoveryPolicy` register row, validated as `z.number().int().positive()` (`packages/register/src/index.ts:444-467`) — the only floor is 1 ms, and no mode-aware minimum exists anywhere. The probe spends `max_tokens: 8` per target per window (`packages/providers/src/provider-probe.ts:82`); the dev seed publishes `600_000` (`apps/runner/src/dev-deployment-register.ts:344`). The NEED is unverified because the exposure is already bounded by the seeded window and by `assertPricedProviderTargets`; and the NUMBER is not REQ's to invent — `docs/architecture/05-register-skeleton.md:506` records provider call bounds as "values — none stated" and `ADR-0015:127-131` bars stating a probe budget outside the register. | `git grep -n probe_freshness_ms -- apps packages tests` · `git grep -n max_tokens -- packages/providers/src/provider-probe.ts` |
| **(e)** an operator acceptance V can run on this Mac | **GAP → S02** | `git grep -n hosted -- acceptance` returns nothing; no file under `acceptance/` names `authorization_file`; every `dev:auth:*` script (`package.json:28-41`) composes the LOCAL stack. A loopback OpenAI-compatible server precedent exists at `acceptance/relay-core.ts:542`. | `git grep -n hosted -- acceptance` · `git grep -ln authorization_file -- acceptance deploy scripts` |

Four GAPs, three slices: (a) → S01, (c)+(e) → S02, (b)+the (d) note → S03.

## Decisions

| date | question | choice | reason | who ruled |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2026-09-24 | Do (a) and (e) belong in one slice, since the acceptance needs a hosted row the publish command writes? | Two slices, S01 then S02, with the dependency declared on S02's second line. | S01 has its own beginning and end V exercises alone — the row IS the product, and V reads the receipt and the `PROVIDER_VENDOR_NOT_VETTED:` refusal back. Folding them makes one slice whose REV(S) covers a publish command AND a TLS fixture AND the dev composition, and the three REV passes are per slice, so a fold spends the cap on unrelated findings. | REQ-PES (default; no V row — this is slicing, not product) |
| 2026-09-24 | Spike shape A — "same refs, different targets": keep the published dev set and swap only the env JSON's `base_url` and `authorization_header` on the VPS. | REJECTED. | `design/spike-2026-09-23.md:30` names the cost itself: refs literally called `development:claude-cli` on a production box, lying in every ledger row. The repo's own boundary test asserts the dev refs are the DEVELOPMENT panel (`tests/architecture/dev-real-provider-only.test.ts:27-31`), and `configured-provider-set.ts:10` seals config as declared, never inferred. V's own research recommended B (`spike:33`). | REQ-PES, recording the spike's recommendation |
| 2026-09-24 | Runtime hostname sniffing — `if (hostname === 'localhost')` inside the API. | REJECTED. | Row V-1's default, and the spike's own reasoning (`spike:37`): it puts "am I local?" into the request path and makes a run's provider lineage depend on ambient machine state. `git grep` finds zero hostname checks today (intake §6, `DEPLOYMENT_KIND` hits: 0). | row V-1 (default binds) |
| 2026-09-24 | A second environment switch beside `DEBATEAI_DEPLOYMENT_MODE`. | REJECTED. | REQ packet charge 5, and the loader already resolves the mode before the first target is read (`packages/providers/src/index.ts:705-718`). A second switch is a second thing to forget. | REQ packet charge 5 |
| 2026-09-24 | Inline credentials on the VPS. | REJECTED, and already impossible. | `deploy/vps/env/runner.env.example:52-55` states the credential is a FILE and an inline `authorization_header` is REFUSED in hosted mode; `deploy/vps/README.md:776` gives the code `PROVIDER_INLINE_CREDENTIAL_REFUSED:`; `tests/unit/v9-provider-credential-files.test.ts:110` pins it. | shipped behaviour (V-9, ruled 2026-09-22) |
| 2026-09-24 | Where does the hosted roster's vendor list come from — a hardcoded module, or the process environment? | The process environment's declared targets, parsed by the SHIPPED `parseProviderDiscoveryTargets` (S01 R1.2a). | A hardcoded roster is a second source of truth for the same set, and the exact-set invariant (`apps/api/src/provider-discovery.ts:55-60`) would then fail by construction whenever the two drift. README:810 also says "V names the vendor" — the operator's env is where V names it. | REQ-PES (default) |
| 2026-09-24 | Where does the V-9(4) vetting record come from — argv, or a file? | A JSON file at `PROVIDER_VENDOR_VETTING_PATH` (S01 R1.2b). | The kit's house style for everything an `EnvironmentFile` carries is a `*_PATH` file (`deploy/vps/env/api.env.example:41-62`), and a JSON array on a systemd `ExecStart` line is unreadable and unrotatable. Vetting dates are not secret, so the file needs no custody mode — which is why this is a plain `*_PATH`, not a `0600` one. Two coders would otherwise build this two ways, so it is pinned here rather than left to ARCH. | REQ-PES (default) |
| 2026-09-24 | `/etc/hosts` vs public DNS for the fake vendor's hostname in S02. | Public DNS: `api.localtest.me`, which resolves to `127.0.0.1` without an edit (S02 R2.6). | `/etc/hosts` needs `sudo` and mutates V's machine, which no acceptance step may do. The cost is a resolver dependency, and S02 R2.6 requires a step that cannot resolve it to report UNVERIFIED rather than work around it. | REQ-PES (default) |
| 2026-09-24 | Does the acceptance publish into the dev Postgres on `:55432`? | No. Every write goes into a scratch database the run creates and drops (S01 R1.12), and the run prints the dev stack's register version before and after to show it did not move. | `:55432` is a NO-TOUCH port carrying a peer session's stack (COMMON §6). A register publication is append-only but still moves the version the peer's `REGISTER_VERSION` is measured against. | COMMON §6 + REQ-PES |
| 2026-09-24 | Should the mission build a probe-freshness floor? | No, not in this mission. S03 R3.6 writes the exposure down; the floor is a `V-ROW: NEW` below. | The number is a register value V ratifies (`05-register-skeleton.md:506`; `ADR-0015:127-131` bars inventing it here), and a requirement whose acceptance depends on an unruled number cannot be exercised by V alone. | REQ-PES (default), routed to V |

## V rows raised by this seat — unnumbered, for the orchestrator to transcribe

`V-ROW: NEW · S01 · REQ t_c677f87a (row V-2 is stale as written)`
Recommended default: **do not build `PROVIDER_DISCOVERY_TARGETS_PATH`.** Row V-2 reads "Hosted
deployments read provider targets (with the Bearer keys) from a 0600 FILE named by
`PROVIDER_DISCOVERY_TARGETS_PATH` … the inline `PROVIDER_DISCOVERY_TARGETS_JSON` stays for
localhost", evidenced by "`runner.env.example:59` (today: inline JSON)". Re-measured, the premise
no longer holds: `deploy/vps/env/runner.env.example:52-55` states each vendor's credential is a
FILE named by `authorization_file` and that an inline `authorization_header` is REFUSED in hosted
mode; `deploy/vps/README.md:776` gives the refusal code; `packages/providers/src/index.ts:757-760`
is the one place a declared credential FILE becomes an in-memory header. So **no key is inline
today**, and `PROVIDER_DISCOVERY_TARGETS_JSON` holds only non-secret target metadata
(`provider_ref`, `base_url`, `model`, `authorization_file`, the two price members). Building a
`_PATH` variant would add a second composition mechanism for a secret that is already out of the
environment — against REQ packet charge 5's "no second mechanism".
Smallest yes/no for V: **"The keys are already in files, not in the env — skip the
`PROVIDER_DISCOVERY_TARGETS_PATH` work?"**
VERDICT: skip it / CONFIDENCE: high (the refusal is shipped and pinned by
`tests/unit/v9-provider-credential-files.test.ts:110`) / STRONGEST COUNTER: a long
`PROVIDER_DISCOVERY_TARGETS_JSON` in an `EnvironmentFile` is still visible in
`/proc/<pid>/environ` to anyone who can read it, and moving the whole array to a file would hide
the vendor list and the model ids too — an inventory disclosure, not a credential one. If V values
that, the work is small and belongs in S02.

`V-ROW: NEW · S03 · REQ t_c677f87a (intake §10 item (d))`
Recommended default: **no probe-freshness floor is built in this mission; S03 R3.6 documents the
exposure instead.** A hosted deployment may publish `panelDiscoveryPolicy.probe_freshness_ms = 1`
(`packages/register/src/index.ts:457` validates only "positive integer"), and each expiry spends
one `max_tokens: 8` completion per target against a paid vendor
(`packages/providers/src/provider-probe.ts:82`). The development seed publishes `600000`
(`apps/runner/src/dev-deployment-register.ts:344`). A minimum is a NUMBER, and
`docs/architecture/05-register-skeleton.md:506` plus
`docs/architecture/01-decisions/ADR-0015-deployment-maker-inventory.md:127-131` put that number in
V's register, not in a seat's SPEC.
Smallest yes/no for V: **"Leave the probe window entirely to the register row you publish, and just
write the cost down?"**
VERDICT: document, do not guard / CONFIDENCE: medium / STRONGEST COUNTER: the row is published by
whoever runs the publish command, and a typo of `1` instead of `1000` is a silent per-ask bill with
no refusal anywhere. A floor V names once would make that typo a boot refusal instead of an
invoice — and if V wants it, it is one requirement in S03 and the number is V's.

## Appended 2026-09-24 by REQ-FIX-PES (node REQ-FIX pass 2 of 3, verdict `../../reviews/REQ-REV-p1.md`) — APPEND-ONLY; nothing above is rewritten

**The SPEC of record for S01 is now `SPEC-v2.md`.** `SPEC.md` stays frozen v1 history. Every
`path:line` above that pointed into `SPEC.md` points into v1 and is read as history; the live
requirements are v2's.

**Correction to the row dated 2026-09-24 "Inline credentials on the VPS" (above).** That row pins
the hosted inline refusal on `tests/unit/v9-provider-credential-files.test.ts:110`. Re-measured:
that case's body only asserts that a credential-FILE target does not throw. The case that asserts
hosted inline credentials throw `PROVIDER_INLINE_CREDENTIAL_REFUSED:` is
`tests/unit/v9-deployment-mode.test.ts:142` (`reviews/REQ-REV-p1.md:51`, N6; the reviewer's probe 8
lists all three `PROVIDER_INLINE_CREDENTIAL_REFUSED` sites). The DECISION is unchanged — inline
credentials are refused in hosted mode — only its citation was wrong. N6 was assigned to the
orchestrator for the V packet; this is the same wrong pin in this file, corrected by appending
rather than by editing the frozen row, because this file is append-only.

| date | question | choice | reason | who ruled |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2026-09-24 | B1: can `parseProviderDiscoveryTargets` be the SOURCE of the hosted row v1's R1.2 asked it to mint? | No. ADDRESSED, not contested: v2's R1.2 replaces it with one declared roster file and a six-row source table, and the parser becomes a CHECK (R1.3) instead of a source. | Measured in the lane: the parser takes the already-published configured set as its second argument (`packages/providers/src/index.ts:232-235`), throws `PROVIDER_DISCOVERY_TARGET_SET_MISMATCH` for any ref that set does not contain (`:295-296`), has no `maker` and no `adapter_kind` in its allow-list (`:264-268`), and returns the configured set's order, not the JSON's (`:333-337`). It is downstream of the row by construction. The row additionally needs `requiredDistinctMakers` and a `sealedSourceRef` (`packages/register/src/configured-provider-set.ts:177-183`), neither of which was an input at all in v1. | REQ-FIX-PES, on `reviews/REQ-REV-p1.md:8-21` |
| 2026-09-24 | Alternative A for B1: add `maker` and `adapter_kind` to the vetting file, keeping two inputs. | REJECTED. | It contradicts the file's own three-field schema and leaves TWO operator-authored sources that must agree about the vendor list — the same class of drift the exact-set invariant exists to catch, moved one step earlier where nothing checks it. | REQ-FIX-PES |
| 2026-09-24 | Alternative B for B1: hardcode `adapterKind: "openai-compatible-http"` and derive `maker` from the ref prefix. | REJECTED. | Two adapter kinds ship (`packages/providers/src/index.ts:807-809`), so a hardcode silently mis-declares a vLLM-served vendor; and a maker derived from a ref string makes DR-013's maker-diversity floor depend on a naming convention no checker enforces. v2 reads `adapter_kind` from the roster and refuses any value not in the shipped `BUILT_IN_PROVIDER_ADAPTERS` constant. | REQ-FIX-PES |
| 2026-09-24 | Alternative C for B1: widen the parser's allow-list so the JSON can carry `maker` and `adapter_kind`. | REJECTED. | It edits the shipped parser both services boot through, which `SPEC-v2.md` §2 forbids and which would change the meaning of every existing `PROVIDER_DISCOVERY_TARGETS_JSON` on any deployed box. | REQ-FIX-PES |
| 2026-09-24 | Where does `requiredDistinctMakers` come from? | The `configuredProviderSet` row at the BASE register version, never the roster file. | A roster file that could set it could LOWER a maker-diversity floor by editing a JSON file, which is exactly the standing-misconfiguration path `ADR-0015:91-96` builds a ledger-derived counter to catch. Reading it from the base row makes the floor unlowerable by this command. | REQ-FIX-PES |
| 2026-09-24 | Where does `sealedSourceRef` come from, and what stops the provenance suffix doubling on a republication? | The base-version row's `sourceRef`, with a trailing `CONFIGURED_PROVIDER_SET_DEPLOYMENT_SOURCE_REF` stripped when present. | `packages/register/src/configured-provider-set.ts:172-175` says the ruling is APPENDED so the row's history reads forward; `:194` appends unconditionally. Without the strip, the second hosted publication carries the suffix twice and the third three times. | REQ-FIX-PES |
| 2026-09-24 | v1's `PES_PUBLISH_SET_ORDER_MISMATCH:` — keep it with a second sequence, or remove it? | REMOVED, and replaced by the shipped-parser self-check `PES_PUBLISH_SET_TARGETS_REJECTED:` (R1.3). | With one source there is no second sequence, so the code could never fire; `slices/S01/PLAN.md` named a different trigger than the SPEC did, which is the fork the verdict names at `reviews/REQ-REV-p1.md:21`. The self-check cannot be vacuous: a duplicate ref, a non-`https:` base URL or a half-declared price all make the shipped parser throw, and the acceptance's `targets-rejected` case fires it with a duplicate ref. | REQ-FIX-PES |
| 2026-09-24 | Is the roster file a "second composition mechanism" that charge 5 of the REQ packet and row V-1 forbid? | No, and R1.13 measures it. | V-1 and charge 5 govern what a BOOTING SERVICE reads to decide its deployment. The roster is read only by a command an operator runs by hand, before any service starts; `apps/api/src/main.ts` and `apps/runner/src/main.ts` still read `PROVIDER_DISCOVERY_TARGETS_JSON` and nothing else, and R1.13 turns that into a grep. This is also why the roster is NOT the withdrawn `PROVIDER_DISCOVERY_TARGETS_PATH` of row V-2. | REQ-FIX-PES |
| 2026-09-24 | N11: intake §10 item (e) ends "a debate ask answered". Does any slice boot a debate? | No. The acceptance of (e) is the shipped discovery PROBE answering and the target joining the panel — one completion, `max_tokens: 8` (`packages/providers/src/provider-probe.ts:82`). | Booting a debate needs an API and a runner, which on this Mac means the NO-TOUCH stack on `:3000`, `:3001` and `:8790` (COMMON §6). `SPEC-v2.md` of S02 states it as an out-of-scope line in §2 as well, so a coder meets it before the acceptance. | REQ-FIX-PES, on `reviews/REQ-REV-p1.md:61` |
| 2026-09-24 | N12 (the scratch database on `:55432`): fix it here? | NAMED, not fixed. | The verdict assigns it to the S01 security lens at REV(S) (`reviews/REQ-REV-p1.md:63`), and this node's packet lists it as not mine. `SPEC-v2.md` §6 names it so the lens finds it. Fixing another node's finding here would also add scope this pass cannot review. | packet REQ-FIX-p2 charge 5 |

