## Appended 2026-09-24 by REQ-FIX-PES (node REQ-FIX pass 3 of 3, verdict `../../reviews/REQ-REV-p2.md`) — APPEND-ONLY; nothing above is rewritten

**The SPEC of record for S01 is now `SPEC-v3.md`.** `SPEC.md` and `SPEC-v2.md` stay frozen history.
The `SPEC-v2 :NN` pointers in the orchestrator's fold above name v2's defective lines and stay true
of the frozen file; the sentences that replace them are, in `SPEC-v3.md`: the inputs table
`:70-75`, the roster gate `:77-92`, the base row `:94-96`, the row-member table `:101-114`, R1.3
`:126-140`, R1.5 `:146-151`, R1.7 `:157-164`, R1.12 `:193-214`, the fixtures and the case table
`:244-270`, the acceptance steps `:272-294`.

**Correction to the pass-2 row "v1's `PES_PUBLISH_SET_ORDER_MISMATCH:` — keep it with a second
sequence, or remove it?" (above).** Its reason says a duplicate ref, a non-`https:` base URL or a
half-declared price "all make the shipped parser throw", and that the `targets-rejected` case fires
the self-check "with a duplicate ref". Executed and re-read at this pass, two of the three are
wrong: a duplicate ref never reaches the parser — the builder throws `CONFIGURED_PROVIDER_SET_INVALID`
first (`packages/register/src/configured-provider-set.ts:82`, via `:184`), which is B1 itself — and
the parser ADMITS `http:` (`packages/providers/src/index.ts:218`); `http:` is refused only by the
hosted boot check (`:646`). The half-declared price does make the parser throw
(`PROVIDER_DISCOVERY_TARGET_PRICE_INVALID`, `:275-279`). The DECISION stands — the order code stays
removed and the self-check replaces it — and its fixture is now a `base_url` ending `/v2`.

| date | question | choice | reason | who ruled |
|---|---|---|---|---|
