`V-ROW: NEW · S01 · REQ-FIX t_690beb44 · Recommended default:` **the hosted publication carries the
`synthesizerRoleRef` and `evaluatorRoleRef` rows forward byte for byte (R1.2, `rows`) and does not
check them against the new provider set.** The development publisher refuses a set that drops a
role's provider (`apps/runner/src/dev-deployment-register.ts:848-858`,
`DEV_ALGORITHM_REGISTER_ROLE_REFS_UNRESOLVED`); SPEC-v3 builds no such check, because no finding
asked for one, pass 3 is the last rework pass, and the acceptance could not exercise it — the seed
of R1.12 holds neither role row (`grep -c RoleRef tests/support/fixtures/register-development-v4.json`
prints `0`). Without the check, the stop is the runner's: every run claimed afterwards fails
terminally with `SYNTHESIS_ROLE_PROVIDER_ABSENT_AT_CLAIM:<role>` (`apps/runner/src/index.ts:2906-2938`).
Smallest yes/no for V: **"Should the hosted publish command refuse a provider set that drops the
provider a synthesizer or evaluator role row names, as the development publisher already does?"**
· VERDICT: carry the rows forward, no publish-time check in this slice / CONFIDENCE: medium /
STRONGEST COUNTER: the check already exists one file away, and without it a hosted operator who
drops the role's provider publishes cleanly and learns of it only when every run on the VPS dies at
claim — once per run, on the box, instead of once at the command where it is cheapest to fix. A yes
is one requirement (a named refusal before the build) and one fixture seeded with role rows.

