`V-ROW: NEW · S01 · ARCH t_96e1881a · Recommended default:` **SPEC-v3 §5 steps 3–6 read the
acceptance command's OWN lines: the lines between pnpm's echo `$ tsx acceptance/pes-accept-publish-set.ts`
(the first line of step 2's `2>&1` log) and, on a failed run only, pnpm's trailer
`[ELIFECYCLE] Command failed with exit code 1.` (the last line); and the acceptance exits 1 on FAIL.**
Measured on pnpm 11.20.0 (probes p3, p4): the echo goes to stderr and `pnpm -s` does not suppress it;
the trailer goes to stdout. §5 lists neither, so a literal reading of step 3 ("the first line is
`PES-S01 SCRATCH-DB …`") fails on every run, and a literal reading of step 6 ("the last line is
`PES-S01-ACCEPT: FAIL …`") fails on every failed run. Smallest yes/no for V: **"May the acceptance's
log start with pnpm's `$ tsx …` line and, when it fails, end with pnpm's `[ELIFECYCLE]` line?"**
· VERDICT: yes, as above / CONFIDENCE: high / STRONGEST COUNTER: a `node --import tsx …` command
line in §5 instead of `pnpm pes:accept-publish-set` prints neither line, at the cost of a longer
command for V to type and a second spelling of the acceptance beside the script.

